\section{Introduction}
This work extends Inverse Link Prediction (ILP-GCN) of Bangian Tabrizi, Jalali \& Houshmand (\textit{J Big Data} 2025) from cheminformatics similarity graphs to attributed social-network sparsification. Novelty claims are restricted by the foundational prior-art analysis; see \texttt{docs/foundational\_analysis.md}.

\section{Related Work}
\subsection{Graph sparsification}
\subsection{Learned graph sparsification (DropEdge, NeuralSparse, PTDNet, DSpar)}
Learning edge importance and pruning is not itself new.
\subsection{Link prediction and Inverse Link Prediction}
Cite ILP-GCN on first mention.
\subsection{Counterfactual graph learning and CF-GNN explanation}
Edge-deletion counterfactuals are established (e.g., CF-GNNExplainer). CAILP uses deletion to estimate \emph{global multi-dimensional harm} under a budget, not to flip a single prediction. This contrast must remain explicit.
\subsection{Edge-centric representation, attention, adversarial learning, representative sampling}
Dual-view attention and Black Hole / GAN modules are design choices or optional hypotheses.

